aperySemigroupRing -- computes the semigroup ring using both the multiplicity and the full Apery set
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        R = aperySemigroupRing L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

While the function semigroupRing L uses just a minimal set of generators, the
function aperySemigroupRing L uses the larger Apery set, and puts the generator
corresponding to the multiplicity at the end.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : L = {5,6}                |
|                              |
|o1 = {5, 6}                   |
|                              |
|o1 : List                     |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : aperySet L               |
|                              |
|o2 = {6, 12, 18, 24}          |
|                              |
|o2 : List                     |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : gens aperySemigroupRing L|
|                              |
|o3 = {x , x , x , x , x }     |
|       1   2   3   4   0      |
|                              |
|o3 : List                     |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : gens semigroupRing L     |
|                              |
|o4 = {x , x }                 |
|       0   1                  |
|                              |
|o4 : List                     |
+------------------------------+

