aperySet -- Compute the apery set of a numerical semigroup
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        as = aperySet L
        aS = aperySet HL
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of positive integers
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, as computed by H =
        apery L
  * Outputs:
      * aS, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

L is taken as generators of a numerical semigroup S; should have gcd = 1. The
apery set is then the list aS = {a_1..a_(m-1)} where m is the smallest element
of L, and a_i is the smallest element of S with a_i = i mod m.

+---------------------------+
|i1 : aperySet {3,5}        |
|                           |
|o1 = {10, 5}               |
|                           |
|o1 : List                  |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : semigroup {3,5}       |
|                           |
|o2 = {0, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10}|
|                           |
|o2 : List                  |
+---------------------------+

