buchweitzSemigroups -- Finds semigroups that are not Weierstrass semigroups by the Buchweitz test
*************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        LL = buchweitzSemigroups g
        LL = buchweitzSemigroups (m,g)
        LL = buchweitzSemigroups (m,c,g)
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, genus
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, multiplicity
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, conductor
  * Outputs:
      * LL, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of semigroups

Description
===========

Uses findSemigroups to produce lists of semigroups with the given invariants,
and then uses the Buchweitz test: the following inequality holds for
Weierstrass semigroups: sums(2, #gaps L) <= dim H^0(\omega_C^{2) = 2*(2g-1) - g
+ 1.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = buchweitzSemigroups (13,26,16)                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {{13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 21, 22, 24}, {13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 22, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     23}}                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : buchweitz 0                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 22, 23}                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = buchweitzSemigroups (14,28,17)                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 23, 24, 26}, {14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     22, 24, 25}}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The second example in these two cases are part of the sequence defined in *note
buchweitz: buchweitz,. As g increases there are many more.

+------------------------------------+
|i4 : #buchweitzSemigroups (15,30,18)|
|                                    |
|o4 = 8                              |
+------------------------------------+

