coneRays -- All the rays of the (homogeneous) Kunz cone
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = coneRays m
  * Inputs:
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, multiplicity
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of ZZ -- columns are vectors
        on the rays of the cone

Description
===========

Uses the Fourier-Motzkin algorithm to compute the rays from the list of
supporting hyperplanes, which is given by *note coneEquations: coneEquations,.
The number of rays grows rather quickly with m; the actual number is unknown.
Use *note facetRays: facetRays, to determine the rays bounding the face on
which a given semigroup lies.

+-----------------------+
|i1 : coneRays 3        |
|                       |
|o1 = | 1 2 |           |
|     | 2 1 |           |
|                       |
|              2       2|
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : coneRays 4        |
|                       |
|o2 = | 1 1 3 1 |       |
|     | 2 0 2 2 |       |
|     | 3 1 1 1 |       |
|                       |
|              3       4|
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : facetRays {4,5,6} |
|                       |
|o3 = | 1 1 |           |
|     | 2 0 |           |
|     | 3 1 |           |
|                       |
|              3       2|
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
