      * D, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, degrees of a basis of
        T^1(semigroupRing L)

Description
===========

T^1(B) is the tangent space to the versal deformation of the ring B, and is
finite dimensional when B has isolated singularity. If B = S/I is a Cohen
presentation, then T^1(B) = coker Hom(Omega_S, B) -> Hom(I/I^2, B). When B is a
semigroup ring, then Henry Pinkham proved that an open subset of the space of
elements of T1 of negative degree correspond to smoothings of the projective
cone of the semigroup ring to Riemann surfaces

+--------------+
|i1 : def1{2,3}|
|              |
|o1 = {-6, -4} |
|              |
|o1 : List     |
+--------------+

