isSymmetric -- test whether the semigroup generated by L is symmetric
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        t = isSymmetric L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * t, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Suppose that c = conductor S, so that c-1 is the last gap. If x in S, and x<c
then c-1-x must be a gap, so the number g of gaps <c is at least the number of
semigroup elements e < c. The semigroup is called \emph{symmetric} if g = e, or
equivalently if the semigroup ring is Gorenstein. Thus for example any
semigroup generated by just 2 elements is symmetric.

+-----------------------+
|i1 : isSymmetric{3,4,5}|
|                       |
|o1 = false             |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : isSymmetric{3, 5} |
|                       |
|o2 = true              |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : gaps {3,5}        |
|                       |
|o3 = {1, 2, 4, 7}      |
|                       |
|o3 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i4 : mu {3,5}          |
|                       |
|o4 = {3, 1}            |
|                       |
|o4 : List              |
+-----------------------+

