knownExample -- Is L a known Weierstrass semigroup?
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = knownExample L
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, genus
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if L is a known
        example of a Weierstrass semigroup

Description
===========

Certain semigroups are known to be Weierstrass. For example L has 2  or 3
generators only, by work of Pinkham and Sally. Another sort examples are
semigroup with small weight ewt(L) < genus L by the work Nathan Pflueger
extending work of Eisenbud-Harris.

