mu -- Compute the point representing a semigroup in the Kunz cone
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        K = mu L
        K = mu H
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, produced by apery L
  * Outputs:
      * K, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

The apery set A of a semigroup s with multiplicity m has the form A_i = i+
mu_i*m. The point with coordinates mu(L) represents semigroup L in the Kunz
cone P_m.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : m = 3                         |
|                                   |
|o1 = 3                             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : L = {3,7}                     |
|                                   |
|o2 = {3, 7}                        |
|                                   |
|o2 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : a = aperySet L                |
|                                   |
|o3 = {7, 14}                       |
|                                   |
|o3 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : b = mu L                      |
|                                   |
|o4 = {2, 4}                        |
|                                   |
|o4 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : apply (#b, i -> (i+1)+(b_i*m))|
|                                   |
|o5 = {7, 14}                       |
|                                   |
|o5 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
